# The settings of the PromoEngine POC stack, read by docker-compose.yml from .env in the same folder (~/bpe/.env).
# install.sh writes .env for you: do not copy this file. It lists every setting with what it is for; it holds no value
# that is a secret, because every secret is made on your machine by install.sh and never leaves .env.

# ---- Written by install.sh from the address you give it (run install.sh again to change them) -----------------------------
# BPE_ORIGIN=https://idea.htcindia.com         the scheme and host people use, without a path
# BPE_URL=https://idea.htcindia.com/bpe        the admin web
# BPE_SHOP_URL=https://idea.htcindia.com/bpe-shop
# BPE_KEYCLOAK_URL=https://idea.htcindia.com/bpe-keycloak   the sign-in; tokens name it as their issuer
# BPE_API_URL=https://idea.htcindia.com/bpe-api            the four services the admin web's pages call
# BPE_PORT=8380                                the one port the stack listens on, on 127.0.0.1 only
# BPE_TAG=latest                               the image version (only when you set it)

# ---- Made by install.sh once, kept on every later run (24 random letters and digits each) -------------------------------
# DB_OWNER_USER=postgres  DB_OWNER_PASSWORD=   the database's owner login
# DB_CONNECTION_LIMIT=10                       connections per service role (a test value)
# KEYCLOAK_ADMIN=admin    KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=   the sign-in server's admin console, at <sign-in address>/admin
# TEST_USER_PASSWORD=                          the password of the five demo people; different on every installation
# PROMO_ADMINISTRATION_CLIENT_SECRET=          the administration service's own sign-in client (reads users for the Users screen)
# PROMO_SEED_CLIENT_SECRET=                    the demo-data job's client; the job deletes that client when it is done
# SVC_PRICING_ENGINE_PASSWORD=  SVC_PROMOTION_AUTHORING_PASSWORD=  SVC_CATALOG_PASSWORD=
# SVC_ADMINISTRATION_PASSWORD=  SVC_AI_ASSIST_PASSWORD=   one database password per service

# ---- Yours to add ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=                              the assistant answers from the live model (OpenAI) when this is set;
#                                              install.sh then writes PROMO_AI_MODE=live, otherwise stub (recorded answers)
# PROMO_AI_MODE=stub|live                      written by install.sh from the line above
